Dear Mayor Orr:
Delta Dental of Wyoming has been pleased to provide the dental benefits to the employees
of City of Cheyenne.
The one year contract for your dental plan ends June 30, 2018.
Pursuant to the provisions of the contract, we are notifying you of the renewal for the new
contract period as stated above. This is a one year contract and a one year rate guarantee.
The new premiums are:
This represents a 0% increase for the above stated contract period.
Based upon the recommendations of the Employee Benefits Committee, the following
proposed enhancements could take effect July 1, 2018: Added coverage for three extra
periodontal cleanings per year (for four total, alternating between Preventive & Diagnostic
and Basic coverage, and in lieu of a regular cleaning), and added coverage for posterior
composites. These new benefits represent a 4% increase, with the following rates:
Please let us know if you have chosen this option by June 1, 2018.
If we do not receive
notification of the change, we will renew the current plan as is with no changes to your
benefits.
Enclosed please find a cost containment report that indicates the dollars saved by Delta
Dental over the last 12 months, and a claims utilization graph. Our cost containment features
have saved $164,127.20, 22.14% of submitted claims or 43.65% of paid claims. You will also
find enclosed a cycle time report indicating the amount of time Delta Dental took to process
each of your claims over the last 12 months.
Please note that 99.6% of your claims were
processed within 15 days.
